And what they see then they never see again. They are particularly moved by the sight of children going to school, blue-grey pigeons swooping down to the pavement from a roof, and rolls dusted with flour being put out by an unseen hand. These rolls, the pigeons, and the two boys are ethereal creatures. All of this happens at the same time: a boy runs towards a pigeon and glances up at them with a smile; the pigeon beats its wings, and flies off, sparkling in the sun, amidst particles of snow shimmering in the air, while from a window comes the smell of freshly baked bread, and rolls are put out… They start laughing and crying with happiness.